      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{68098a4626271974ef4d2775|full_name} compiling shaders and loading the world is happening mostly on CPU, but it's the GPU that goes to 100%. You can see on the screenshot the performance overlay shows 169 fps, in less demanding worlds it goes up to a few hundred. It's literally like disabling V-Sync and just letting your GPU render as many frames as it can.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
