      "sourceFeatureExtractionItemID": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I'm pretty sure it's VRChat doing the rendering? Specifically rendering the desktop view (I was recently made aware about early desktop loading screens worlds can implement). I'd imagine it's because there is no output to the headset happening during the loading screen, so the frame rate is unbound.\n\nAs far as I know SteamVR is rendering the simple loading screen at the refresh rate of the headset, so it can only be VRC, and given the above, I think it makes sense there is just no cap on FPS.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
